  "title": "Codex MCP OAuth fails on both /mcp URL variants; CLI reports Premium Archive as Free",
  "summary": "I am a Premium Archive subscriber, but cannot authenticate NewsBlur MCP with Codex on macOS. With this Codex configuration: [mcp_servers.newsblur] url = \"https://newsblur.com/mcp\" I get: Error: Metadata error: Protected resource metadata resource mismatch: reference 'https://newsblur.com/mcp', permitted 'https://newsblur.com/mcp/' With the trailing slash: [mcp_servers.newsblur] url = \"https://newsblur.com/mcp/\" I get: Error: Authorization server issuer mismatch: expected https://newsblur...",
